<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sino-Indian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1962</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sino-Indian War was a border war fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in October and November 1962 over disputed Himalayan territory in Aksai Chin and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-east-frontier-agency">North-East Frontier Agency</a>. Chinese forces overran Indian positions on both fronts, then declared a ceasefire and withdrew in the east while keeping Aksai Chin. The defeat damaged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawaharlal-nehru">Jawaharlal Nehru</a>'s prestige and led India to expand and modernise its armed forces.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sino-indian-war.jpg" alt="Sino-Indian War" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indian_soldiers_on_patrol_during_the_1962_Sino-Indian_border_war.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
